# FABLE-SONNET-OWN-LOOKUP-AUDIT-20260923-131 Part 2 (b): re-verifying
# l2_prep's l2_own_find_last call (tried FIRST there, l2_own_find only as
# its fallback) against -129's fallback. `x` is a unit field, passed AS A
# CALL ARGUMENT from inside a nested method -- backward-visible per the
# author's norm. Since -129 gave l2_own_find_last the same unit-fallback
# l2_own_find already had, whichever of the two actually resolves `x`
# here, the chain as a whole must still find it -- this fixture confirms
# that (see the -131 Part 2 report for the resulting redundancy note: the
# second try in this pair can now never add anything the first didn't
# already cover).
int: x 5

fn: helper (int: n) int
    return: n
end: helper

fn: bump () int
    return: helper(x)
end: bump

int: r
r: bump()
if: r != 5
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 90; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
